    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e71cc7c_a6d603f1",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 42
      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-22T03:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Andrey had brought up the communication being over dbus, but I think we agreed it wasn\u0027t worth generating this extra key pair to encrypt the data being sent to citadel because an attacker with enough access to sniff DBUS could just capture the keystrokes.",
      "parentUuid": "1bf5a40a_14154465",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "48465188afa886efe6a381147ee8a452b9f88992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02be4479_7cc8f099",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 42
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-20T15:12:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should we also include the sizes to avoid encoding ambiguity?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "48465188afa886efe6a381147ee8a452b9f88992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "545dedef_fe621d34",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 42
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-22T03:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t want to complicate the protocol by accepting any version of struct wrapped_leaf_data for any message type that passes struct wrapped_leaf_data. I have moved the version field to the very beginning of the struct so an upgrade function can infer the lengths and structs from that field. If future versions have variable length structs, the length fields should be added then, but it doesn\u0027t make sense to add unnecessary length fields because they are a common source of programmer error.\n\nI have updated this function to take pointers and lengths as parameters, but a new message should be created when the first protocol change is made for upgrading leaves from older versions to the current version. The handler for that can use the updated version of this function.",
      "parentUuid": "02be4479_7cc8f099",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "48465188afa886efe6a381147ee8a452b9f88992",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dabd130_64e6720a",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 42
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-20T15:12:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, this code is probably easier to read if we do a child_hash-\u003etemp_hash memcpy first, then the loop, then a temp_hash-\u003enew_root memcpy.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 105,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 105,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "48465188afa886efe6a381147ee8a452b9f88992",
